Bind pyjnius to Flet's libpyjni instead of SDL.

Upstream's Android wheel looks for SDL's JNIEnv getter, then for
JNI_GetCreatedJavaVMs (API 31+). A Flet app has no SDL, so neither works below
API 31. libpyjni's JNI_OnLoad, run by serious_python, captures the JavaVM and
the app ClassLoader.

PyJni_FindClass goes through that ClassLoader. Raw JNI FindClass on a thread
Python attached uses the system loader, which cannot see the app's own classes.

The glue is a new file because jnius_jvm_android.pxi has CRLF endings, which GNU
patch will not match against an LF hunk. setup.py hardcodes the android platform
because upstream only detects it from python-for-android's environment.

